Negative control for the per-panel url namespace (RT1).

An area stacks several collections on one page and each owns the same params
(`sort`, `limit`, `offset`, `filter.*`, `track`). A panel's view of the url bag
prefixes every param it writes with its key (`links.sort`), so two panels never
share one. This mutant leaves the READ side namespaced and writes bare params:
a panel's criteria go into the url as `sort=…`, where no panel reads them back
and every other panel's write overwrites them — the first reload loses the
filters of all but the last panel to write.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Expected red (module lane): criteria-url-roundtrip.spec.ts — a criteria write
made under a panel namespace must reach the url as `<panel>.<param>` and must
round-trip into the same panel only.

